course: dictionary
lesson: 11728
title: Avert: stop it or look away
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Avert has two meanings. The first is to stop something bad from happening: «The driver braked hard and averted a crash.» No crash happened because of the quick braking, so avert means stopped.
explain: The second meaning is to look away. «When the scary part came on screen, Mia averted her eyes.» Mia did not want to see, so she turned her eyes away. Here avert is about your eyes or your gaze.
explain: Avert is a slightly formal word, so you will meet it more in stories and the news than in everyday chat. A good check is to swap in stop or look away and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Avert means to stop something bad from happening, as in «avert a disaster».
fact: «Avert your eyes» means to look away, often because something is upsetting or embarrassing.
fact: Avert is a slightly formal word, so it is more common in stories and news.
fact: Useful phrases: avert disaster, avert a crisis, avert your eyes.
fact: When avert means stop something bad, the thing being stopped is usually bad, such as a crash, a disaster or a crisis.
exercise: «Quick thinking averted a disaster at the river bank.» What does averted mean here? | Watched closely | Forgot | Caused | *Stopped from happening
exercise: «Mia averted her eyes from the scary film.» What does averted her eyes mean? | Opened them wide | Closed her eyes tightly to sleep | Stared at it | *Looked away
exercise: Which word is a formal verb in «The firefighters averted a crisis by closing the valve in time.»? | *averted | valve | closing | firefighters
test: «The guard shouted, and the thief's plan was averted.» What does averted mean? | Celebrated | Copied | Started early | *Stopped from happening
test: Ben averted his gaze when the teacher looked at him, because he was shy. What does averted his gaze mean? | Shouted an answer | Waved at the teacher | *Looked away | Ran out of the room
exam: Which sentence uses avert to mean stop something bad? | The cat averted its eyes from the bird | *Quick action averted a flood in the village | Sam averted his face when he got the joke | Mum averted her eyes at the cooking smell
